;; Endeavour 155 rung 02 — EVERY A/B operand of an fp16 register tile must be fp16.
;;
;; WHY THIS RUNG EXISTS WHEN 01 ALREADY COVERS 16-BIT TILES.  It does not cover the same thing.
;; Rung 01 asserts that a 16-bit type reached the module and that SOME cooperative matrix uses it.
;; That assertion is satisfied by a module in which MOST operands are still float32 — and that is
;; the module Crisp emits today.  The weak form was written to catch "the element type was
;; discarded"; it cannot see "the element type was discarded ON SOME PATHS", which is the defect
;; that is actually present.
;;
;; WHAT THE EMITTED MODULE LOOKS LIKE RIGHT NOW.  Disassembling this kernel's .spv shows every
;; operand declared TWICE, once per component width, with no conversion ops between them:
;;
;;     id 360  component=32-bit  A            <-- wrong
;;     id 363  component=16-bit  A
;;     id 372  component=32-bit  B            <-- wrong
;;     id 374  component=16-bit  B
;;     id 383  component=32-bit  Accumulator  <-- correct, an fp16 MMA accumulates in fp32
;;
;; and the f32 operand types are referenced MORE than the f16 ones (42/22 vs 18/10 in the
;; benchmark kernel).  So the majority of fragments still compute in the wrong precision.  On BMG
;; this is worth ~50x: the fp16 top-chapter kernel measures 0.27 TFLOPS at N=4096 where the tf32
;; kernel measures 16.33 and oneMKL fp16 measures 110.38.
;;
;; NEW VALIDATOR: validate-spv-fp16-coop, which asserts the invariant a mixed-precision MMA
;; actually has — every A-use and B-use cooperative matrix is 16-bit, every Accumulator is fp32 —
;; rather than "at least one of them is 16-bit somewhere".
;;
;; WHY fp16 AND NOT bf16 CARRIES THE 16-BIT COVERAGE.  bf16 cannot be loaded on the BMG driver at
;; all: the Level Zero SPIR-V reader (IGC 1.6.33578) does not implement SPV_KHR_bfloat16, reports
;; `input SPIR-V module uses unknown extension`, and then crashes.  That is a driver gap, not a
;; Crisp defect — three independent translators accept the same module.  fp16 goes through the
;; IDENTICAL typed path and DOES load and run, so fp16 is what makes 16-bit MMA testable end to
;; end on Intel.  Rung 01 stays bf16 and compile-only; this rung is the one that can go to metal.
;;
;; THE --hardware-profile FLAG IS REQUIRED, and I initially thought it was not.  The reasoning was
;; that :mma-shapes is only checked when a profile is active and this rung asserts a TYPE, not a
;; shape — so the flag could be dropped and rung 01's forwarding gap (obstacle 3) sidestepped.
;; The compiler says otherwise, and says it clearly:
;;
;;     load-tile into a register-tile requires a hardware profile (pass --hardware-profile):
;;     its GRF / L1 limits drive the register-pipeline safety analysis.
;;
;; Which is right: a register tile's legality depends on how many registers the part HAS, and that
;; is a property of the profile, not of the shape literal.  Recorded because it is a real constraint
;; on every register-tile spec, not a quirk of this one.
;;
;; ===================================================================
;; STATUS: RED ON PURPOSE, and beyond ci-stop.  This is a TDD rung stating a defect that is
;; present in the compiler today.  It goes green when the f32 A/B cooperative-matrix types stop
;; being minted.  Move ci-stop to 155-typed-mma-shapes when the whole directory passes.
;; ===================================================================
;;
;; SKIP-DEFAULT-PASS
;; SKIP-WITH[--differentiate]: "AD mints no adjoint for register tiles bound INSIDE a tile-stride body (Unknown variable C-TILE_ADJ); hoisting the identical bindings to the enclosing let compiles clean. NOT a 16-bit gap -- a tf32 twin fails identically."
;; TEST-WITH[--ir-target=spv --hardware-profile=bmg] : validate-spv-fp16-coop
(declaim (precision fast))
(def-type a-mat (matrix half  :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))
(def-type b-mat (matrix half  :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))
(def-type c-mat (matrix float :address-space :global :align :compact :contiguous-term :row-major))

(def-kernel fp16_tile (A B &out C)
  (declare #'(a-mat b-mat &out c-mat)
           (global-size :derive-from C :strategy :strided)
           (local-size :set-to 16))
  (let ((K (inner-dimension A B)))
    (tile-stride C (8 16) (grid-y grid-x)
      (let ((A-tile (make-register-tile half  (8 16)  0.0 :operand :a))
            (B-tile (make-register-tile half  (16 16) 0.0 :operand :b))
            (C-tile (make-register-tile float (8 16)  0.0)))
        (dotimes (grid-k (/ (to-ulong K) (to-ulong 16)))
          (load-tile A A-tile (grid-y grid-k))
          (load-tile B B-tile (grid-k grid-x))
          (mma-accumulate-via-tile (8 16 16) C-tile A-tile B-tile))
        :epilogue
        (store-tile C-tile C (grid-y grid-x))))))
